     "page": 1,
     "text": "Reeves-Rodriguez Clinic\nRe: David Sawyer (DOB 11/27/1977)\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nI am writing this letter at the request of Mr. David Sawyer regarding his medical history, specifically his treatment for Alcohol use disorder.\n\nMr. Sawyer was last seen on May 14, 2025. He presented for his routine follow-up regarding his Alcohol use disorder, which he has been treating successfully. His pressure was 132/65 and his weight was 179 pounds. His condition is stable, and he continues to do well with no recent relapses. He is currently taking acamprosate 333 mg daily as part of his treatment regimen.\n\nOn August 30, 2024, Mr. Sawyer was seen again for his Alcohol use disorder. His blood pressure was 143/69 and his weight was 177 pounds. He has been abstinent for 4.7 years and is actively participating in outpatient treatment and AA meetings. He has experienced no relapses during this period.\n\nHis most recent lab review was on December 16, 2023. At that time, his blood pressure was 136/72 and his weight was 179 pounds. His Alcohol use disorder remains in controlled status, with no recent issues reported.\n\nIn April 2023, Mr. Sawyer visited for back strain. His blood pressure was 137/63 and his weight was 166 pounds. Despite this minor complaint, his Alcohol use disorder continues to be well-managed, with no relapses noted since his treatment began.\n\nIn July 2022, Mr\n"
